\nRETINA thresh0.25 centre tower:eye-tower-g2 sqrt unit   # EYE GENE = Alpha 3's SEALED EYE TOWER (E09d seed 20260913 \u2192 E46d arm (b) MERGED-1, adopted\n                                     #   2026-09-16 17:3x, /data/dev/alpha3/judge/eye-tower-g2, sha 6abc6d75\u2026): conv 8@5x5 \u2192 ReLU \u2192 2x2 max \u2192 conv 7@3x3\n                                     #   \u2192 ReLU \u2192 4x4 mean \u2192 112 features. FIXED during a life (never learned here). Before it: a contrast floor and the\n                                     #   ink's centroid to the centre (the tower was trained on centred glyphs; G0b \u00a72b); after it: a fixed square root,\n                                     #   unit length. Proof: the C++ organ replays E09d's 2,356 held-out frames byte for byte; the numpy road is gated on\n                                     #   that seal's own features (genome/eye.py, run log).\nSENSE  ear    letters 8              # words on a page: 8 slots x 27 symbols = 216, unit length (Alpha 2 lexicon HEADWORDS reused the same letters)\nAREA   sight  from retina\nAREA   words  from ear\nMEET   sight  words                  # rung 0: the meeting is EDGES ONLY (the neural organ's W between two populations, E48b arm A1)\n# GROW \u2014 E48b's arm-A1 rule, ported byte-exact into Alpha 3's neural organ and alive three days (SOLUTIONS #227; NOTES 09-16 20:24)\nBIRTH  novelty  cos<0.576          # no cell resonates -> a new cell holds the input (GWR's novelty birth; THETA_N from gate G-a, never by habit)\nBIRTH  error    misfires 3           # a cell keeps answering wrongly -> a new cell is born beside it (E48b's error birth)\nBUDGET 400 per arrival               # a budget that REFUSES, never a cap that eats the least-used (E48 \u2192 E48b, #227); refusals printed\nNMAX   2000\n# WIRE \u2014 Hebb between co-active areas, a delta rule that shrinks what is WRONG (E48b; the neural organ)\nKWTA   5                             # five winners per area per moment (E48b's k-winners; a winner must resonate, G0 \u00a711 am. 3)\nHEBB   window 1                      # cells active in the SAME moment across areas get an edge (his 09-16 18:46 \u00absimultaneous inputs that MEET\u00bb)\nDELTA  lr 0.05                       # the edge grows when the pairing is right, shrinks when wrong (E48b's delta rule)\n# SHRINK \u2014 the wrong and the redundant, never the merely unused (#227: shrinking by disuse IS forgetting)\nPRUNE  w<0.02 after 3 chances        # E48b's floor\nMERGE  cos>0.9975 same-answer       # D41 (c): merge redundant units \u2014 shrinking that costs no retention\nSCALE  every 1000 moments            # HOMEOSTASIS = Alpha 1's plasticity program, M3 homeostasis 192/192 (the one plasticity primitive that carried)\n# STAGE \u2014 critical periods (his 09-16 18:46: reading \u2192 sentences \u2192 paragraphs; senses first)\nSTAGE  1 senses   moments 0..200\nSTAGE  2 meet     moments 200..\n# ANSWER \u2014 from the grown structure only; the truth stays outside (Alpha 2's belief-scope law)\nRECALL k=1                           # light one side as a moment does, read the strongest edge (G0 \u00a711 am. 6)\nABSTAIN second/best > 0.85           # \u00abI do not know this\u00bb when a COMPETITOR is too close (G0 \u00a711 am. 5); metacognition's first cell (F4)\n#\n# DECLARED, OFF IN THIS RUN \u2014 each is an estate organ with a proof; each gets its own run, one at a time (PREREG \u00a71b):\nGAZE   surprise fixations 4 grid 16 canvas 128 glance 32 ink border     # GAZE GENE ON (G1 \u00a71): Alpha 2 organs/retina.py + organs/gaze.py (V0.1, d772bf7, 2026-09-05) imported VERBATIM,\n                                     #   sha-pinned in genome/gaze.py; fixation 1 = the saliency peak, then the most surprising unvisited cell (residual saliency on a\n                                     #   first frame), inhibition of return, 4 per picture (12 was per page frame); a glance = a 32\u00d732 window on the fixated cell; INK (\u00a76 am. 1) =\n                                     #   |grey \u2212 median of the window's 2-px rim| / max (\u00a76 amendment 1; the first run's |grey \u2212 mean| rule made filled shapes one shape); each glance is one moment with the same word. Proof: V0.1's 12 regions vs the random twin's 3\u20134.\n#OFF EAR-SOUND cochlear gammatone agc      # E52's cochlear front (Alpha 3, 09-17): the first hearing gate PASS at 1.000; its ablation says the loudness path carries \u2014 for the sound sense\n#OFF CONTEXT   family read-time            # D31 (Alpha 3, 09-16): the family as read-time context \u2014 digits 0.692 \u2192 0.792, handwritten 0.193 \u2192 0.660; here the WORD is the picture's context\n#OFF CURIOSITY interest-population         # Alpha 2 organs/curiosity_genome.py (L2, 09-01): content-free operators, beat its null twin every measurement (16,114.6 vs 2,223.3) \u2014 for when he chooses his own stream\n#OFF PREDICT   next-moment error           # his research (the AGI Q&A \u00a7predictive coding / active inference; R2): he says what comes next and files the miss \u2014 the error signal that closes no loop over his own records (F1)\n#OFF SENTENCE  compose under-judge         # Alpha 2 speech_v2 (L4, 09-02): sentences composed from his own record under a frozen judge, never next-token; his 09-12 12:38 \u00abspeaks as an organism\u00bb\n#OFF HANDS     jail landlock seccomp       # Alpha 2 core/jail (A2-R6), reused by Alpha 3's hands: the road to run what he writes; the open world (his 09-17 00:07)\n\n# G3 (docs/G3-LAWS-PREREG.md): two laws changed, one gene added \u2014 on Ahmad's 19:19 \u00abLet's tweak some genome laws\u00bb / 19:30 \u00abOk go\u00bb\nRESONATE sight nearest words cos>=0.9   # sight winners = the nearest KWTA cells at or above the FLOOR (THETA_N := between-p5, gate G-a); words keep a strict threshold\nABSTAIN  margin cos<0.0189              # \u00abclose\u00bb: the best-answering lit cell must beat the best lit cell of a different answer by MARGIN (gate: 5 % of the band width)\n# gate G-a wrote THETA_N=0.576 THETA_M=0.9975 MARGIN=0.0189 \u2014 G3 floor rule [toy first-fixation glances (G3-toy)]: THETA_N = between-p5; MARGIN = 5 % of the band width 0.3790; within-median 0.9554 between-p95 0.9064; seed 20260919\n", "state_hash": "a2875ffa6fd47d54583c5425b5e1deb173ea8f64e5baf06a34875c092e9c2353"}